# Role Templates and Enablement (ticket 08).
# Platform Admin requests need a Platform Admin access token (see http/platform-applications.http).
# Tenant Admin requests need an access token with an Active Tenant (see http/tenants.http).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:9800
@platformToken = paste-platform-admin-access-token
@tenantToken = paste-tenant-admin-access-token
@applicationId = paste-application-id
@templateId = paste-role-template-id
@permissionId = paste-template-permission-id

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Role Templates (Platform Admin, platform audit chain)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Create a Role Template, optionally with Permissions. Each must name an Action on a Resource Type
### in the Application Schema that isn't Deprecated (400 otherwise). inverted: true is a Deny Rule.
### 409 if the name exists in this Application (ignoring case).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}/role-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Editor",
  "description": "Reads and edits invoices, never exports them",
  "permissions": [
    { "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "read" },
    { "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "approve" },
    { "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "export", "inverted": true }
  ]
}

### The Application's Role Templates, oldest first (paginated: limit, cursor).
### Permissions on Deprecated Resource Types or Actions have "deprecated": true.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}/role-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### Rename or re-describe. Tenants' copies don't change.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}/role-templates/{{templateId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Invoice Editor" }

### Add a Permission (409 if the template already has it)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}/role-templates/{{templateId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "read", "inverted": false }

### Remove a Permission, including one on a Deprecated entry
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}/role-templates/{{templateId}}/permissions/{{permissionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### Delete a Role Template (204). Roles already copied from it stay.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}/role-templates/{{templateId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enablement (Tenant Admin of the Active Tenant, Tenant audit chain)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Every registered Application, oldest first, with enabled, enabledAt, disabledAt and the count of
### this Tenant's Permissions that use Deprecated entries (paginated: limit, cursor)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### One Application: its Schema, the Tenant's Roles for it (Deprecated Permissions flagged) and, before
### the first Enablement, the Role Templates that enabling will copy
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/applications/{{applicationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Enable. The first time copies the Role Templates in as Roles (skipping Permissions on Deprecated
### entries). Enabling again after a disable brings back the Tenant's Roles as they were, copying nothing.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/applications/{{applicationId}}/enable
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Disable. The Tenant's Roles for it are kept.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/applications/{{applicationId}}/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### The Enablement changes in the Tenant's Audit Log
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/audit-events?applicationId={{applicationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
